## 0. Mission

Stand up a new Go service `siem-service` in the Clario360 monorepo that boots cleanly under the **existing** `bootstrap.Bootstrap` pattern, exposes `/healthz`, `/readyz`, `/metrics`, registers under the API gateway at `/api/v1/siem`, ships baseline schemas in a new `siem_db` database, extends the platform RBAC catalogue, and is wired into the local dev stack (Docker, ecosystem manager, Prometheus). At the end of this prompt the service must be **live, observable, authenticated, and idle** — no business endpoints yet, but the next 29 prompts must be able to start building on top of it without touching any of this foundation again.

The deliverable is **production-grade and reversible**. Every change must come with passing tests at three levels (unit, integration, regression-of-existing-services), and the existing platform must build, test, and run identically with the service disabled as it does today.

