## 6. Anti-patterns / pitfalls (the agent must self-check against this list before submitting)

- ❌ Using `prometheus.DefaultRegisterer` anywhere. Registering on the default registry once contaminates every later test.
- ❌ Calling `context.Background()` inside an HTTP handler chain.
- ❌ Swallowing errors with `_ = err`. Every error is either returned, logged with `zap.Error(err)`, or both.
- ❌ Hardcoded ports, URLs, or DSNs in code. All come from config.
- ❌ A goroutine spawned without a context-cancel exit path or a `sync.WaitGroup` join.
- ❌ Mounting `/api/v1/siem/_meta` outside the auth+tenant middleware. There are no anonymous SIEM endpoints, period.
- ❌ Adding a `siem:*` wildcard permission. Wildcards are forbidden — RBAC is permission-by-permission.
- ❌ Writing a migration that is not idempotent or has no `.down.sql`.
- ❌ Bypassing the platform error mapper to return ad-hoc JSON errors.
- ❌ Logging the JWT, the JWKS, or any header named `Authorization`, `Cookie`, `X-Api-Key`.
- ❌ Introducing a new Go dependency without justification in `RECON.md`. Prefer what is already in `go.mod`.
- ❌ Touching any file outside the deliverables manifest in §8 without explicit justification.

